  "2026-09-18T23:36:15.493Z","harness:codex","Delivery scope: singleton persistence semantics are SDK-owned and shared by CLI/MCP. Existing per-file schema mutation locks and default lifecycle predecessor retention were verified against closed canonical history before editing. No public SDK exports or contract shapes changed. Hard-link publication intentionally refuses unsupported filesystems rather than overwriting concurrently created schema bytes; full-document settings replacement remains explicit for caller-constructed objects."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T23:18:45.361Z","harness:codex",Atomic rename prevents torn bytes but cannot prevent a stale read-modify-write from losing a peer edit. Reconcile tracked settings snapshots inside the history lock; serialize session mutations; publish schema seeds without replacing an existing pathname; reject non-identical checkpoint ID reuse.
